        "authorName": "Codebrew Software & Evgeny Zinoviev & Felipe Gonzalez",
        "name": {
          "en-US": "Gravity Defied Classic"
        },
        "summary": {
          "en-US": "Iconic retro trial racing motorcycle game"
        },
        "description": {
          "en-US": "Gravity Defied: Trial Racing is a legendary physics-based trial motorcycle racing game originally developed by Codebrew Software in 2004 for J2ME mobile devices.\n\nThis modernized Android edition faithfully preserves the authentic 2004 fixed-point physics engine, classic wireframe vector tracks, and responsive bike dynamics while introducing comprehensive updates for contemporary smartphones.\n\nFeatures of this modernized edition:\n• Complete collection of all 30 original classic tracks across 100cc, 175cc, 220cc, and 325cc leagues.\n• Integrated mod catalog with in-game downloading and instant switching between over 1000 fan-made track packs.\n• Virtual on-screen 1–9 numeric control pad with multi-touch and haptic feedback.\n• Edge-to-edge layout with full support for modern display cutouts and aspect ratios.\n• Complete removal of proprietary telemetry and tracking SDKs (Firebase/Crashlytics) for complete privacy and libre compliance.\n• Modernized Android toolchain targeting Android 15/16+ (SDK 35/36).\n• Compatible with all modern 64-bit devices and 16 KB page-size kernels.\n• Free and open-source under the GPL-2.0 license.\n"
        },
        "icon": {
